silm:instances_papers_17_commutative_diagrams_as_governance_chapters_03_discoverable_contradictions_sections_02_violation_as_typed_data_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'ViolationAsTypedDataConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, the concrete embodiment of ']' in the Mittens domain: the body-mass quality bearing 4.7 kg, the vet record signed at 10:00:03 by Dr. Chen, the microchip UID 985112, or the auth-log line under policy CAT-17 on 2026-05-18 -- pinned to the running cat example, never to a bare letter.; also, the concrete embodiment of 'ContractClause' in the Mittens domain: the body-mass quality bearing 4.7 kg, the vet record signed at 10:00:03 by Dr. Chen, the microchip UID 985112, or the auth-log line under policy CAT-17 on 2026-05-18 -- pinned to the running cat example, never to a bare letter.; also, the concrete embodiment of 'ViolationReport' in the Mittens domain: the body-mass quality bearing 4.7 kg, the vet record signed at 10:00:03 by Dr. Chen, the microchip UID 985112, or the auth-log line under policy CAT-17 on 2026-05-18 -- pinned to the running cat example, never to a bare letter.." .
